59:52.449 --> 59:55.683
Item 7A is an ordinance of Eagle Mountain City, Utah,

59:55.892 --> 59:59.194
amending the official zoning map and future land use map

59:59.723 --> 01:00:03.201
to a commercial storage and business park,

01:00:03.586 --> 01:00:06.744
light industrial. So with that,

01:00:07.337 --> 01:00:10.815
Vicki. Thank you. Just wait on the

01:00:11.315 --> 01:00:15.015
screen here. Okay, so this is

01:00:15.192 --> 01:00:19.126
an applicant-initiated proposal Just some brief history on

01:00:19.159 --> 01:00:21.952
the property. So back in April,

01:00:23.393 --> 01:00:26.719
DAI came up and requested with City Council

01:00:27.313 --> 01:00:30.832
how they felt about a proposed storage, self-storage facility.

01:00:31.668 --> 01:00:35.186
They did receive positive feedback and were encouraged to proceed with the application.

01:00:36.092 --> 01:00:39.988
And then in July, we talked about a lot split application, which was approved

01:00:40.150 --> 01:00:43.720
by Planning Commission. And so that split

01:00:43.785 --> 01:00:46.588
off that original lot is what this application is for. For today,

01:00:47.138 --> 01:00:50.065
and they are doing the rezone, a general plan amendment,

01:00:50.453 --> 01:00:54.112
and a development agreement. The property

01:00:54.612 --> 01:00:58.641
in question, this is here. So it's currently zoned agriculture.

01:00:59.124 --> 01:01:02.364
They'd like to change it to commercial storage. Makes the most sense for a self-storage

01:01:02.412 --> 01:01:05.791
facility. The surrounding zoning I have listed

01:01:06.291 --> 01:01:08.892
here as well. So residential to the north with the Harmony MDA,

01:01:09.808 --> 01:01:13.278
agriculture to the south and to the west, and then there is a community commercial

01:01:13.778 --> 01:01:16.713
lot to the east. That was rezoned back in 2021.

01:01:19.319 --> 01:01:22.796
One small hiccup with the zone compatibility determination, one of

01:01:23.296 --> 01:01:26.957
the requirements for approval. The R table does list

01:01:27.216 --> 01:01:31.488
what's compatible for the commercial storage zone, and the surrounding uses

01:01:32.005 --> 01:01:35.450
are not that for the north, the west, and the south. But because these

01:01:35.547 --> 01:01:38.877
are legislative decisions, we've covered this in the past, they're not legally

01:01:39.377 --> 01:01:43.094
required to be compatible. It is a preference, so I just wanted to make

01:01:43.594 --> 01:01:47.399
sure that that was clear. The future land

01:01:47.899 --> 01:01:51.400
use designation will change with this proposal as well. So it's currently Neighborhood Residential

01:01:51.432 --> 01:01:54.935
1, and it's proposed to upgrade to the Business Park/Light

01:01:54.967 --> 01:01:58.599
Industrial, which is compatible between the zone and the future

01:01:59.099 --> 01:02:03.030
land use designation. And on the current screenshot,

01:02:03.046 --> 01:02:06.600
the UDOT freeway alignment, that's that dark red line off

01:02:07.100 --> 01:02:11.261
to the the left-hand side of the map, that it's an old alignment. So keep

01:02:11.761 --> 01:02:14.938
that in mind here. On our Transportation Master Plan,

01:02:15.051 --> 01:02:18.728
that dark blue line, dashed line, that's the updated

01:02:19.228 --> 01:02:22.357
alignment. And so you can see the proximity of the proposed parcel to

01:02:22.857 --> 01:02:26.852
the freeway. Given that we're working on the General Plan, that's likely all

01:02:27.352 --> 01:02:30.561
going to change. And so we think that this is a useful rezone for that

01:02:34.783 --> 01:02:38.521
For the criteria, the changes to the general plan maintain that

01:02:38.569 --> 01:02:42.147
compliance that's necessary. We covered that compatibility

01:02:42.179 --> 01:02:46.319
determination needed. There's not going to be a major change in need for city services.

01:02:46.977 --> 01:02:50.411
And for traffic generation, while David Salazar was still here,

01:02:50.523 --> 01:02:54.342
he had reviewed the proposal and he didn't have any concerns regarding

01:02:54.358 --> 01:02:58.064
the traffic generation. And the applicant did say when they presented

01:02:58.564 --> 01:03:01.829
to city council that they anticipate roughly 13 trips per per day, so pretty

01:03:02.329 --> 01:03:05.774
minimal impact there. And then for the property value changes,

01:03:05.968 --> 01:03:08.184
we don't anticipate a significant change there.

01:03:09.679 --> 01:03:12.188
And staff recommends that you forward a positive recommendation.

01:03:18.020 --> 01:03:19.657
Any questions for staff?

01:03:25.545 --> 01:03:28.066
Okay. Would the applicant like to come up?

01:03:29.096 --> 01:03:32.965
Hi, Planning Commissioners. Chase Andreasi

01:03:33.078 --> 01:03:35.117
with BAI and Candlelight Homes. Um,

01:03:35.952 --> 01:03:39.067
thank you for having us here tonight. We're excited by this location.

01:03:39.982 --> 01:03:43.563
Um, as, as Mickey pointed out, you know, there's future growth that's happening.

01:03:43.755 --> 01:03:46.838
There's changes where the highway is going to be, the freeway is going to be,

01:03:47.432 --> 01:03:50.740
and we think this is a useful site. Um, as you may know, we're also

01:03:51.240 --> 01:03:54.433
developing Firefly, and this site is kind of in between the growth

01:03:54.933 --> 01:03:56.968
we've got going there, growth you see on the other side of the city.

01:03:57.786 --> 01:04:01.925
And as we all know, as you build out, we see less

01:04:02.054 --> 01:04:05.824
and less garages, fewer and fewer garages being used for storing cars

01:04:06.324 --> 01:04:10.220
and more for storing, you know, all of your stuff. And so

01:04:10.720 --> 01:04:13.910
we have seen a strong, um, correlation between the need for sites

01:04:14.410 --> 01:04:17.777
like this to help people store things. Um, so not only would it

01:04:18.277 --> 01:04:20.809
benefit what we're doing out in Firefly, but other parts of the city as well

01:04:20.986 --> 01:04:24.902
in terms of providing additional space for storage. It's a unique site.

01:04:25.142 --> 01:04:28.754
It's very long, not very deep, and those are

01:04:28.786 --> 01:04:32.397
tough and difficult at times to plan. Um, and so

01:04:32.525 --> 01:04:35.751
we have found in other parts of the state this

01:04:36.251 --> 01:04:40.774
is a particularly good use for those kind of interesting sites. And again,

01:04:40.806 --> 01:04:44.738
given the future growth and development that's going to occur and will continue

01:04:45.238 --> 01:04:49.186
occurring here, we just are excited by this site and look forward to

01:04:49.715 --> 01:04:53.473
moving forward with it. So happy to answer any questions you have. I don't

01:04:53.489 --> 01:04:57.246
want to oversell what, what Mickey already did, but she

01:04:57.746 --> 01:05:01.084
covered it all. So, um, any questions?

01:05:02.464 --> 01:05:06.238
Is this just like unit storage, or would this be trailer

01:05:06.738 --> 01:05:10.557
storage, RV storage? Both. Great question. Yeah, so there's, there's 2 phases that we have

01:05:10.589 --> 01:05:14.441
planned. And the reason we do this in phases is we'll build out,

01:05:14.666 --> 01:05:18.469
I think the first phase, 75,000 square feet of self-storage.

01:05:18.534 --> 01:05:22.241
So the garages roll up different sizes that people can choose from,

01:05:22.787 --> 01:05:25.740
and that will kind of be the perimeter. The benefit of doing that along the

01:05:26.240 --> 01:05:29.832
perimeter is that establishes also your fence. Yeah. So if you have a

01:05:29.993 --> 01:05:33.299
use on the other side, it's no different than putting up a precast fence

01:05:33.799 --> 01:05:37.311
between Use A on this property and Use B on the other property.

01:05:37.909 --> 01:05:41.403
So we build that around the perimeter, and then in

01:05:41.597 --> 01:05:45.366
the middle, we would have temporary

01:05:46.369 --> 01:05:49.672
RV storage until phase 1 was built up,

01:05:49.768 --> 01:05:53.408
stabilized. We had, you know, all the spaces leased up, and then

01:05:53.456 --> 01:05:56.864
we would come in with a phase 2 potentially and build out additional

01:05:57.364 --> 01:06:00.877
storage— self-storage, I should say. So that was

01:06:00.910 --> 01:06:04.575
the long answer to your question. The answer is yes, we do both.

01:06:04.912 --> 01:06:08.348
Yeah, RV storage in the middle, self-storage on the outside.

01:06:09.007 --> 01:06:12.154
Yep. Any other questions? Commissioner Allen? Yeah,

01:06:12.250 --> 01:06:16.152
so it looks like Pole Canyon will eventually be a major arterial, so 5

01:06:16.168 --> 01:06:19.540
lanes. I'm assuming you have enough setbacks so for future expansion

01:06:20.040 --> 01:06:22.205
of the road you're not going to have to move anything, correct? Yeah, we've got—

01:06:23.072 --> 01:06:26.942
we're dedicating almost 25% of the actual depth

01:06:27.442 --> 01:06:30.749
of the lot for Pole Canyon. So one of the deviations that

01:06:30.781 --> 01:06:34.172
we are asking for is to go from 25 to

01:06:34.638 --> 01:06:38.173
20 feet in the front setback. And the reason

01:06:38.673 --> 01:06:41.965
for that, again, is your wall. The wall is actually the back

01:06:42.029 --> 01:06:46.191
of your storage unit. So if you were to put a commercial— a precast

01:06:46.691 --> 01:06:49.582
wall around a commercial property in the same spot,

01:06:49.726 --> 01:06:53.438
that's just establishing where your self-storage is going to start.

01:06:53.840 --> 01:06:57.834
So. Okay, any other

01:06:58.334 --> 01:07:02.074
questions? Commissioner Jensen? Does, does the back of a storage

01:07:02.171 --> 01:07:04.686
unit meet a fencing code?

01:07:07.051 --> 01:07:10.665
So again, how this has worked in other cities, and I believe it works this

01:07:10.923 --> 01:07:14.941
way in your city code as well, is that operates as a

01:07:14.957 --> 01:07:18.332
fence, the back of the storage, because it's minimum 6 feet high.

01:07:19.031 --> 01:07:22.465
It's a precast material or a CMU material,

01:07:22.870 --> 01:07:26.182
and so it acts as your fence. Was that, was that

01:07:26.280 --> 01:07:28.647
the question? Yeah, that is my question. Okay.

01:07:29.468 --> 01:07:32.915
Yeah. Okay. That is, that is specifically

01:07:33.415 --> 01:07:36.007
addressed in the development agreement, which is the next item on the agenda.

01:07:38.023 --> 01:07:41.593
Perfect. Any other questions? More just

01:07:42.093 --> 01:07:45.195
a comment. I know we're just looking at the zoning change, which I have no

01:07:45.695 --> 01:07:49.980
problem with that at all, but, uh, Just since my brain goes on from a

01:07:50.180 --> 01:07:53.780
development and an appraisal standpoint, just even

01:07:54.280 --> 01:07:55.960
though we're growing like crazy and I don't think it would be a problem,

01:07:56.220 --> 01:07:59.400
just making sure, you know, I think a lot of people bring in storage facilities

01:07:59.900 --> 01:08:02.899
that they think are just ready to go and they're feasible,

01:08:03.399 --> 01:08:07.820
and then we show them that it's not. And there's— that's probably 95%

01:08:08.320 --> 01:08:11.900
or more of the storage that we look at right now is not feasible for

01:08:12.400 --> 01:08:15.362
new construction just because they're going in areas where there's A lot, a lot of

01:08:15.747 --> 01:08:19.424
supply already, and we've been adding quite a bit of supply of storage here to

01:08:19.924 --> 01:08:22.732
keep up with our growth, of course, and we'll need it as we continue to

01:08:23.232 --> 01:08:26.120
grow, I'm sure. Yeah, but just making sure that that's something that you guys are

01:08:26.620 --> 01:08:28.722
looking at too, and you have those feasibility studies done just to make sure you're

01:08:28.738 --> 01:08:32.576
in a good spot, which it seems like you are. So we go— great question.

01:08:32.672 --> 01:08:35.868
We go through pretty extensive market studies

01:08:36.060 --> 01:08:39.513
and a market analysis. This is Extra Space branded,

01:08:39.673 --> 01:08:43.462
right? So we are working with Extra Space They don't sign off on

01:08:43.962 --> 01:08:46.833
a site until they've done all of that. The good thing is, and hopefully we

01:08:47.333 --> 01:08:50.669
never have to get there, these are also pretty easy to redevelop, right? It's a

01:08:50.734 --> 01:08:54.265
couple of CMU buildings that you knock down at the end of the day and

01:08:54.765 --> 01:08:57.507
you can put something else up if the market changes on you. Yeah,

01:08:57.973 --> 01:09:00.589
perfect. Any other questions?

01:09:01.889 --> 01:09:02.243
Perfect.

01:09:06.801 --> 01:09:10.943
Turned it off. This is a public hearing, so at

01:09:11.280 --> 01:09:14.315
6:45 we will open the public hearing.

01:09:14.830 --> 01:09:19.270
Have we had any feedback from— on internet

01:09:19.770 --> 01:09:23.255
or anything else? Is there anybody here that would like to address

01:09:23.838 --> 01:09:24.825
us on this item?

01:09:28.327 --> 01:09:31.764
Okay. At 6:45, we will close the public hearing.

01:09:32.527 --> 01:09:35.830
So any discussion on this we need from—

01:09:35.896 --> 01:09:38.466
No. Okay.

01:09:39.519 --> 01:09:41.585
With that, I will entertain a motion.

01:09:44.793 --> 01:09:48.087
Chair, I move that we forward a positive recommendation to the City Council

01:09:48.184 --> 01:09:50.147
for Item 7A as presented.

01:09:51.500 --> 01:09:54.906
I'll second that. Okay, uh, the— there's been a

01:09:55.406 --> 01:09:59.149
motion made by Commissioner Allen, seconded by Commissioner

01:09:59.649 --> 01:10:02.580
Freeh. Uh, we will start the, uh,

01:10:04.307 --> 01:10:07.655
voting with Commissioner Strong. So Commissioner Strong

01:10:08.155 --> 01:10:11.733
is a yes. Commissioner Allen? Yes. Commissioner Free?

01:10:12.038 --> 01:10:15.152
Yes. Uh, Commissioner Jensen? Yes.

01:10:15.811 --> 01:10:19.519
Commissioner Dkorski? Yes. That is 5-0,

01:10:19.824 --> 01:10:21.413
and that motion passes.

01:10:22.585 --> 01:10:24.496
Okay,

01:10:25.860 --> 01:10:28.284
with that, we will go on to item 7B,

01:10:29.633 --> 01:10:33.148
ordinance— an ordinance of Eagle Mountain City Utah approving

01:10:33.164 --> 01:10:37.070
the development agreement with Ranch House Storage

01:10:38.920 --> 01:10:42.056
LLC. There really isn't much to add here from the last

01:10:42.556 --> 01:10:45.961
presentation. This is just the development agreement that's going

01:10:45.978 --> 01:10:49.616
along with it. So looking

01:10:50.116 --> 01:10:53.231
in, I guess, Section 5, you look at the different— 5.1

01:10:53.989 --> 01:10:57.588
talks about the intended uses are self-storage and outdoor vehicular storage.

01:10:58.779 --> 01:11:02.485
And, you know, accessory uses of office space as well

01:11:02.985 --> 01:11:06.324
for that use. Again, the design standards are

01:11:06.824 --> 01:11:10.099
attached relative to that.

01:11:10.323 --> 01:11:13.728
And the fencing again is addressed. It indicates the locations

01:11:14.228 --> 01:11:18.017
of that, including that that's gonna be abutting the property line with the building acting

01:11:18.033 --> 01:11:21.036
as the fence. So that's, but yeah,

01:11:22.305 --> 01:11:25.742
setbacks are addressed. I think it's 19 feet, not 20, as the front setback that

01:11:26.242 --> 01:11:30.279
was requested. Um, a deviation from the 25 feet. With that

01:11:30.327 --> 01:11:34.157
being said, our code actually allows us to deviate. It's specifically built into the code

01:11:34.657 --> 01:11:38.051
in this zone to, uh, if it's approved by the city council,

01:11:38.500 --> 01:11:41.785
if it finds that the reduced setback's not interfered with the use, enjoyment, and character

01:11:42.285 --> 01:11:45.406
of adjacent properties. If it makes that finding, then that's actually not against the code.

01:11:45.486 --> 01:11:49.669
It's allowed by code to deviate from the setbacks. Um, and that's

01:11:49.941 --> 01:11:52.329
really it. Uh, as you indicated, there'll be phasing.

01:11:53.279 --> 01:11:57.218
Um, there's, you know, going to be upsizing Pole Canyon Boulevard

01:11:57.718 --> 01:12:00.951
to the arterial road standard that needs to be in that location.

01:12:01.581 --> 01:12:03.878
And that's really it. This is pretty straightforward.

01:12:04.526 --> 01:12:08.604
Okay, perfect. Um, any questions

01:12:08.717 --> 01:12:09.720
